 \section{Conclusions}
-Complete inference from validated logged token lengths yields reproducible lexical scores for an instrumented T5 reconstruction pipeline. Five archived-reference series have means of 0.482--0.535; two additional archived series remain diagnostics because of malformed word boundaries. Separate experiments with verified detokenization yield mean scores of 0.435 for TinyLlama and 0.504 for Phi-3.5-mini. They strengthen the need to distinguish observation validity from reference validity and are not combined into an intrinsic seven-model vulnerability ranking.
